          "@value": "Interest Income, Federal Funds Sold",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": [
        {
          "@value": "Interest income on federal funds sold. Federal funds sold represent the excess federal funds held by one commercial bank which it lends to another commercial bank, usually at an agreed-upon (federal funds) rate of interest. Such loans generally are of short-duration (overnight).",
          "@language": "en"
        }
